invariant: INV-14
file: src/jws.c
catches: jws_test
reason: verify_rs256 takes a modulus below 256 bytes. RFC 7518 section 3.3
  requires a key of 2048 bits or more for RS256, and jws.h states the
  floor so that no caller has to repeat it. The check then accepts a token
  under a 2040-bit key. Every other token verifies as before, so only a
  key one byte under the floor shows it: test/gen_jws_vectors.py signs a
  token under one with OpenSSL, and bin/jws_test requires CH_EINVAL for
  it.

--- old
        k.n_len < CH_JWS_RSA_MODULUS_LEN_MIN || k.n_len > CH_JWS_RSA_MODULUS_LEN_MAX ||
--- new
        k.n_len > CH_JWS_RSA_MODULUS_LEN_MAX ||
